You are a senior full-stack developer building a production app for LEAFY KEYS, a private security company in Kenya. Build a mobile-first app with two modules: (1) a Digital Occurrence Book (OB) for static guards, and (2) Daily E-Bike Patrol Reports. It must integrate with our existing Leafy Keys Guard App.

## 1. Users and roles (role-based access)
- Static Officer: writes OB entries for their assigned site and shift only.
- E-Bike Rider and E-Bike Crew Member: each patrol has exactly one rider and one crew member. Both must log in and confirm they are on the patrol.
- Supervisor: views and approves reports for their sites and bikes, and receives alerts.
- Operations / Control Room: live view of all sites, patrols and incidents.
- Admin: manages users, sites, bikes, checkpoints, shifts and settings.
- (Optional) Client: read-only access to the daily reports for their own site.

## 2. Module A – Digital Occurrence Book (static officers)
- Shift start: officer logs in, selects or is assigned a site, and records the handover from the previous officer (items, keys and equipment received, outstanding issues). The incoming officer confirms receipt.
- Entry types: Routine/Patrol round, Incident, Visitor in/out, Vehicle in/out (plate number), Delivery, Key issued/returned, Alarm activation, Power/water outage, Police/emergency services visit, Equipment fault, Handover, Other.
- Every entry records automatically: server timestamp (EAT, UTC+3), the officer's ID, site, GPS location, and the device time. It can also include free text, photos (compressed), and an optional voice note.
- Entries are APPEND-ONLY. They can never be edited or deleted. Corrections are made as a new "Amendment" entry linked to the original, with a reason. Keep a full audit trail.
- Running entry numbers per site per day, like a paper OB.
- A panic/emergency button that alerts the supervisor and control room with the officer's GPS location.
- Shift close: the officer signs digitally. The system then generates the Daily Site OB Report (PDF), and the supervisor reviews and approves it.

## 3. Module B – Daily E-Bike Patrol Report
- Patrol start: select bike (by ID or registration number). Rider and crew member both confirm they are on the patrol.
- Pre-ride checklist: battery %, odometer reading, tyres, brakes, lights, horn, mirrors, helmets for both people, reflective gear, radio/phone charged. Include photos of the bike. Any failed item blocks the patrol until a supervisor overrides it, and the override is logged.
- During patrol: GPS track is recorded at a sensible interval to save battery. Checkpoint scans use a QR code (optionally NFC) at each patrolled location. Incidents, suspicious activity and stops are logged using the same entry format as the OB. The panic button is available.
- Missed or late checkpoints trigger an alert to the supervisor.
- Patrol end: battery %, odometer reading, km covered (calculated automatically and checked against the odometer), any damage or faults, and charging status.
- Generate the Daily E-Bike Patrol Report (PDF): crew, bike, times, route map, checkpoints hit or missed, incidents, km, battery used, and bike condition.
- Bike fleet records: maintenance log, faults reported, and service due (by km).

## 4. Supervisor / Control Room dashboard (web)
- Live map of active patrols and staffed sites.
- Alerts feed: panic, missed checkpoints, no OB entry for X minutes (configurable), and failed bike checks.
- Search and filter all entries by date, site, officer, bike or entry type.
- Approve daily reports. Export to PDF and Excel. Optionally email reports to clients automatically.
- Basic analytics: incidents per site, patrol completion rate, km per bike, and bike faults.

